This is a port of Quake, originally created by webOS Internals. Updated in 2026 by codepoet and webOS Archive to add Bluetooth and USB Controller Support.

http://www.libsdl.org/projects/quake/

The source code is from http://www.libsdl.org/projects/quake/src/sdlquake-1.0.9.tar.gz


================================================================================
CONTROLS
================================================================================

Three input methods work at once: the on-screen touch overlay, a USB or
Bluetooth game controller, and a USB or Bluetooth keyboard. Plug a controller or
keyboard in at any time -- they are picked up within about a second, with no
need to restart the game.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KEYBOARD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are Quake 1.09's own stock bindings. NOTE: there is no WASD -- movement is
on the arrow keys, which is how Quake shipped in 1996. See "Rebinding" below if
you want WASD.

  Movement
    Up Arrow / Down Arrow      Move forward / backward
    Left Arrow / Right Arrow   Turn left / right
    Alt (hold) + Left/Right    Strafe instead of turn
    , and .                    Strafe left / right
    Shift (hold)               Run
    Space or Enter             Jump
    D / C                      Swim up / down

  Combat
    Ctrl                       Fire
    1 - 8                      Select weapon directly
    /                          Next weapon

  Looking
    A / Z                      Look up / down
    Page Down / Delete         Look up / down
    End                        Centre the view
    Insert (hold)              Keyboard look
    \ (hold)                   Mouse look

  Interface
    Esc                        Menu
    ` (backtick)               Console
    Tab                        Scoreboard
    T                          Chat message
    Pause                      Pause
    - / =                      Shrink / enlarge the view
    F1                         Help
    F2 / F3                    Save / Load menu
    F4                         Options menu
    F5                         Multiplayer menu
    F6 / F9                    Quicksave / Quickload
    F10                        Quit
    F11                        Zoom in
    F12                        Screenshot

Every printable key, arrow, function key and modifier reaches the game, and
holding Shift produces capitals and shifted symbols when typing in the console.
Verified with a Mitsumi/Apple Extended USB keyboard; a Bluetooth keyboard
paired through webOS should work the same way, as it arrives over the same
/dev/input path.

Rebinding: open the console with ` and use Quake's normal bind command, for
example

    bind w +forward
    bind s +back
    bind a +moveleft
    bind d +moveright

Bindings are saved to id1/config.cfg and persist across launches.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GAME CONTROLLER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

One scheme is used for every supported pad, so muscle memory carries between
them. Positions below are described physically; CONTROLS.md gives the exact
button for each pad, and CONTROLS.csv is the machine-readable table.

  In game
    Left stick, D-pad          Move and strafe
    Right stick                Look
    Face buttons               Look left / down / right / up
                               (so aiming works on pads with no right stick)
    Left shoulder              Jump
    Right shoulder             Fire
    Left trigger               Run (hold)
    Right trigger              Next weapon
    Stick clicks               Run
    Start                      Menu
    Back / Select              Previous weapon

  In menus
    D-pad, left stick          Navigate
    Right side of the pad      Select
      (face-down, face-right, right shoulder/trigger/stick-click)
    Left side of the pad       Back
      (face-left, face-up, left shoulder/trigger/stick-click, Back, Start)

No in-game action fires while a menu is open.

Verified pads: Sony DualShock 4 (USB and Bluetooth), ShanWan "Xbox knock-off"
wireless, DragonRise "Sega Saturn style" wireless, and the Logitech Precision
Gamepad. Other pads fall back to a generic profile that follows the standard
evdev button names and should work without configuration.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TOUCH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The on-screen overlay drives the menus as well as the game: the fire button acts
as Select, the top edge of the screen acts as Escape, and the on-screen stick
moves the menu selection.
